{
  "name": "TestReportMasksSensitiveVariables",
  "comment": "Proves test.report writes an assertion failure through the diagnostic face, so a\nsensitive value is masked. The fixture fails with an Identity (carrying a sensitive\nPrivateKey) as the failure's Actual and in the Variables snapshot. The written\nreport content keeps the key name ('privateKey') with its value masked ('****'),\nwhile the non-sensitive 'publicKey' still serializes. A regression that writes the\nvalue itself would fail the '****' assertion.",
